    {
      "name": "BandInvitation",
      "views": [
        {
          "actions": [
            "read",
            "search"
          ],
          "comment": "The invitee's side of an invitation, and the only screen in this app a\nperson who belongs to no band can do anything on. `MyInvitationList`\nabove is its admin-facing mirror -- that one is `CONTEXT REQUIRED Band`\nand lists what a band has *sent*; this one is `CONTEXT ALL Band` and\nlists what the caller has *received*, across every band a\n`pendingBandInvitation` grant or a membership can reach.\n\nAccept only. Giggle Band declares no `DeclineBandInvitation`, so unlike\nJointly Care's `MyPendingInvites` there is no second row action to pair\nwith it; the object already models `Status: 'Declined'` and its\n`respondedAtRequiredAfterResponse` validation already anticipates the\ntransition, so adding one is a product decision rather than a platform\ngap.\n\nThe list carries `FILTER Status == 'Pending'` rather than the read model\ndoing it: an invitation that has been accepted, declined or revoked is\nstill the caller's to see, and keeping the filter on the surface leaves\n`MyBandInvitations` reusable for a history screen without loosening a\npolicy to get it.\n\nIts `SHELL NAV` item carries no visibility predicate, deliberately. Every\nother `Main` item is gated on `CONTEXT SELECTED Band`, which is exactly\nwrong here: the person this screen exists for has joined no band and has no\nreason to open a context picker, and `CONTEXT ALL Band` is precisely what\nmeans no selection is needed. A caller with no invitation reaches it and\nsees the declared empty state, which is a cheaper failure than a nav item\nhidden from the only person who needs it. Mirrors Jointly Care's \"My\nInvites\" -- group `Main`, order 15, unguarded.",
          "context": {
            "context": "Band",
            "mode": "all"
          },
          "fields": [
            "Band",
            "Role",
            "Status",
            "SentAt"
          ],
          "kind": "dashboard",
          "name": "MyBandInvitationList",
          "presentation": {
            "iconMaps": [],
            "legends": [],
            "sections": [
              {
                "calendars": [],
                "controls": [],
                "heading": "Your invitations",
                "lists": [
                  {
                    "actions": [
                      {
                        "command": "AcceptBandInvitation",
                        "comment": "`WHEN Invitee == RUNTIME.userId` keeps the button off rows the\ncaller is not the invitee of, which this list also carries: a\n`BandAdmin` sees their own band's outgoing invitations here too\n(see `MyBandInvitations` in `domain.adlj`), and\n`AcceptBandInvitation`'s own `REQUIRE Invitee == RUNTIME.userId`\nstep guard would refuse the click anyway. Same reasoning as the\n`revoke` action's `WHEN Status == 'Pending'` above. `INPUT\nInvitation FROM id` carries the row's own record identity, the\ntoken Phase 69 added for exactly this.",
                        "icon": {
                          "kind": "named",
                          "name": "check"
                        },
                        "input": {
                          "Invitation": "id"
                        },
                        "kind": "action",
                        "label": "Accept",
                        "name": "accept",
                        "placement": "row",
                        "visibleWhen": "Invitee == RUNTIME.userId"
                      }
                    ],
                    "density": "compact",
                    "emptyState": {
                      "text": "No invitations yet. When a band invites you, it appears here."
                    },
                    "filter": "Status == 'Pending'",
                    "name": "MyInvitationsList",
                    "row": {
                      "fragments": [
                        {
                          "field": "Band",
                          "kind": "field",
                          "style": "bold"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": " - invited as "
                        },
                        {
                          "field": "Role",
                          "kind": "field"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": " on "
                        },
                        {
                          "field": "SentAt",
                          "format": {
                            "kind": "date",
                            "pattern": "EEE d MMM"
                          },
                          "kind": "field"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "sort": [
                      {
                        "direction": "asc",
                        "field": "SentAt"
                      }
                    ],
                    "source": "MyBandInvitations"
                  }
                ],
                "name": "Invitations"
              }
            ],
            "state": [],
            "statusMaps": [],
            "statuses": []
          },
          "readModel": "MyBandInvitations",
          "searchFields": [],
          "sort": [
            {
              "direction": "asc",
              "field": "SentAt"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "actions": [
            "read",
            "search"
          ],
          "comment": "Admin-facing counterpart to the `HomeDashboard` \"Invitations\" feed, which\nonly ever shows what is still `Pending`. `RevokeBandInvitation` exists and\nis exercised directly (see `band-reference-app.test.ts`), the same way\n`AcceptBandInvitation` has been since Phase 28; the `revoke` row ACTION\nbelow is what wires a one-click button to it. This was blocked until\nPhase 69: a presentation `ACTION`'s `INPUT ... FROM \u003cexpr\u003e` only ever saw\na row's already-projected field values, with no way to reach a row's own\nrecord identity (`meta.guid`) -- see `docs/spec/language.md`'s \"Composed\nView Presentation\" section for the `id` token Phase 69 introduced to close\nexactly this gap, and `duplicateGig` above for the `PLACEMENT row` shape\nthis action reuses.",
          "context": {
            "context": "Band",
            "mode": "required"
          },
          "fields": [
            "InviteeEmail",
            "Role",
            "Status",
            "SentAt",
            "RespondedAt"
          ],
          "kind": "dashboard",
          "name": "MyInvitationList",
          "presentation": {
            "iconMaps": [],
            "legends": [],
            "sections": [
              {
                "calendars": [],
                "controls": [],
                "heading": "Sent invitations",
                "lists": [
                  {
                    "actions": [
                      {
                        "command": "RevokeBandInvitation",
                        "comment": "`WHEN Status == 'Pending'` keeps the button off rows that cannot\nactually be revoked (already accepted, declined, or revoked), even\nthough `RevokeBandInvitation`'s own `REQUIRE Status == 'Pending'`\nstep guard makes this safe either way -- offering it everywhere\nwould just invite a confusing server-side rejection for no reason.",
                        "icon": {
                          "kind": "named",
                          "name": "x"
                        },
                        "input": {
                          "Invitation": "id"
                        },
                        "kind": "action",
                        "label": "Revoke",
                        "name": "revoke",
                        "placement": "row",
                        "visibleWhen": "Status == 'Pending'"
                      }
                    ],
                    "density": "compact",
                    "emptyState": {
                      "text": "No invitations sent yet"
                    },
                    "name": "SentInvitationsList",
                    "row": {
                      "fragments": [
                        {
                          "field": "InviteeEmail",
                          "kind": "field",
                          "style": "bold"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": " - "
                        },
                        {
                          "field": "Role",
                          "kind": "field"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": " - "
                        },
                        {
                          "field": "Status",
                          "kind": "field"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": " - "
                        },
                        {
                          "field": "SentAt",
                          "format": {
                            "kind": "date",
                            "pattern": "EEE d MMM"
                          },
                          "kind": "field"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "sort": [
                      {
                        "direction": "desc",
                        "field": "SentAt"
                      }
                    ],
                    "source": "SentBandInvitations"
                  }
                ],
                "name": "SentInvitations"
              }
            ],
            "state": [],
            "statusMaps": [],
            "statuses": []
          },
          "readModel": "SentBandInvitations",
          "searchFields": [],
          "sort": [
            {
              "direction": "desc",
              "field": "SentAt"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Availability",
      "views": [
        {
          "actions": [
            "read",
            "search"
          ],
          "comment": "`BandMemberAvailabilityBoard` keeps its whole-band roster (the `Availability`\nsection, backed by `BandMemberAvailability`, unchanged) and adds a second:\nthe signed-in member's own schedule, overlaid with gigs booked with *any*\nband they belong to, not just the one currently selected. A gig-derived\nstatus outranks a plain availability status on the same date -- the same\n`PRECEDENCE 100` device `BandEventCalendar`'s `conflict` status already\nuses, reused here so a real booking outranks a stale \"I'm free\" note on\nthe same date.\n\nThe label deliberately says \"Gig booked\" rather than naming which band:\na read-model expression only ever sees `RUNTIME.userId` / `RUNTIME.now`\n(see `docs/spec/language.md`'s Read Models section), never which business\ncontext the *consuming view* currently has selected, so nothing here can\ntell the currently-selected band's own gig apart from another band's. Both\nare still correctly \"booked\" -- the wording just does not overclaim which\none.",
          "context": {
            "context": "Band",
            "mode": "required"
          },
          "fields": [
            "Member",
            "Role",
            "Date",
            "Status"
          ],
          "kind": "dashboard",
          "name": "BandMemberAvailabilityBoard",
          "presentation": {
            "density": "compact",
            "iconMaps": [],
            "legends": [],
            "sections": [
              {
                "calendars": [],
                "comment": "`Availability`, not `Who is free`: `TeamAvailabilityList` carries no\nfilter, so the section lists every member's availability including\n`Unavailable` rows. The roster is deliberate -- the heading was the part\nthat overclaimed. The view's nav item stays distinct (`Band Availability`)\nbecause `MyAvailabilityList` already owns the `Availability` nav label,\nand two identical nav entries would be worse than either wording.\n\nThe view also declares no `LEGEND`. Each status carries a distinct colour\n*and* a distinct icon (`calendar` vs `x`) plus an `ARIA_LABEL`, so the\nencoding is never colour-only and a legend explains nothing the cells do\nnot already say.",
                "controls": [],
                "heading": "Availability",
                "lists": [
                  {
                    "density": "compact",
                    "emptyState": {
                      "text": "No availability recorded yet"
                    },
                    "name": "TeamAvailabilityList",
                    "row": {
                      "fragments": [
                        {
                          "field": "Member",
                          "kind": "field",
                          "style": "bold"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": " - "
                        },
                        {
                          "field": "Role",
                          "kind": "field"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": " - "
                        },
                        {
                          "field": "Date",
                          "format": {
                            "kind": "date",
                            "pattern": "EEE d MMM"
                          },
                          "kind": "field"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": " - "
                        },
                        {
                          "field": "Status",
                          "kind": "field"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "sort": [
                      {
                        "direction": "asc",
                        "field": "Date"
                      }
                    ],
                    "source": "BandMemberAvailability"
                  }
                ],
                "name": "TeamAvailability"
              },
              {
                "calendars": [
                  {
                    "dateField": "ScheduleDate",
                    "density": "compact",
                    "emptyState": {
                      "text": "Nothing scheduled this month"
                    },
                    "fields": [
                      "ScheduleDate",
                      "ScheduleStatus",
                      "Title",
                      "VenueName"
                    ],
                    "month": {
                      "state": "visibleMonth"
                    },
                    "name": "MyScheduleCalendar",
                    "sort": [
                      {
                        "direction": "asc",
                        "field": "ScheduleDate"
                      }
                    ],
                    "source": "MyAvailabilityWithGigs",
                    "sourceKind": "readModel",
                    "status": {
                      "candidates": [
                        {
                          "field": "ScheduleStatus",
